#: ../../quick_start.rst:2
msgid "Quick Start"
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:4
msgid ""
"This walks a Zotero library from nothing to searchable full text and a "
"citation network. Each step is resumable — interrupting a batch and re-"
"running it picks up where it stopped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:9
msgid "1. Connect Zotero"
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:11
msgid "Settings → **Zotero** tab → enter ``user_id`` and API key → OK."
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:13
msgid ""
"The app syncs on startup and whenever you press **Sync** in the left "
"rail. Collections appear as a tree under the *My Library* tab; papers "
"show in the middle list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:17
msgid ""
"The first sync only fetches metadata. PDFs stay in Zotero until they are "
"needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:20
msgid "2. Run OCR"
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:22
msgid ""
"Right-click a collection → **Process Folder (OCR → Biblio)**, or right-"
"click *My Library* → **Process All** for the whole library."
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:25
msgid ""
"The Process window shows progress per file. Each PDF is downloaded, sent "
"to the OCR backend, and its text stored page by page. Results are cached "
"in ``~/.papermeister/ocr_json/``, so re-processing a paper is free."
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:29
msgid "Watch the status pill in the paper list:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:35
msgid "Pill"
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:36
msgid "Meaning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:37
msgid "``wait``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:38
msgid "PDF present, not processed yet"
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:39
msgid "``OCR``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:40
msgid "text extracted, no bibliographic data yet"
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:41
msgid "``done``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:42
msgid "metadata extracted and applied"
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:43
msgid "``rev``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:44
msgid "extracted metadata disagrees with Zotero — needs your review"
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:45
msgid "``err``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:46
msgid "processing failed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:47
msgid "``skip``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:48
msgid "not a PDF (supplementary file, link attachment)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:49
msgid "``—``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:50
msgid "no PDF attached"
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:53
msgid "3. Extract bibliographic data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:55
msgid ""
"If automatic extraction is on, this follows OCR without any action. "
"Otherwise right-click a paper → **Extract Biblio**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:58
msgid ""
"The result is stored in a separate table, never written over your Zotero "
"data directly. When the extraction agrees with what Zotero already has, "
"or fills empty fields only, it is applied automatically. When it "
"conflicts, the paper is marked ``rev`` and waits for you."
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:63
msgid ""
"To review: select the paper, open the **Metadata** tab, and compare the "
"two columns field by field. Pick a side per row, edit the value if "
"neither is right, then **Apply**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:68
msgid "4. Parse reference lists"
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:70
msgid ""
"Right-click a paper, a collection, or *My Library* → **Extract "
"References**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:72
msgid ""
"Each paper's bibliography is located, split into entries, and parsed into"
" structured fields. Entries are then matched against papers you already "
"hold — by DOI first, then by title with author and year as corroboration."
" Everything else becomes an external *cited work*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:77
msgid ""
"The **References** tab of a paper shows both directions: works it cites, "
"and papers in your library that cite it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:81
msgid "5. Search"
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:83
msgid ""
"Type in the search box and press Enter. Search covers the full OCR text "
"of every page, plus titles and author names, so a paper is findable by a "
"term that never appears in its body."
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:87
msgid ""
"Results show a snippet with the matched words in bold; opening a result "
"highlights the matches inside the **Text** tab."
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:91
msgid "6. See the citation network"
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:93
msgid ""
"Right-click a paper → **Show in citation network** for an interactive "
"graph centred on it: what it cites, what cites it, and the external works"
" it cites. Click any node to re-centre."
msgstr ""

#: ../../quick_start.rst:97
msgid ""
"The rail's **Cited Works** view lists external works by how often your "
"library cites them — a direct answer to \"what do I keep citing but not "
"own?\""
msgstr ""

